description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/patch-with-tools.ts, add the deterministic vacuous-edit check to this patcher's landing path.

WHY. patch_with_tools self-lands via the mitosis cutover and does not run feature_compose's semantic gate. Its one location check, regionContainmentVerdict, is deliberately "gated ONLY when the proposal names a region" - and measured 2026-09-10, only 113 of 4,357 gaps carry a region (93 of 1,050 open ones). So for roughly 91-97% of proposals this path lands with typecheck as its only substantive check. Commit 6dc2005 is what that permits: two const declarations that nothing reads, landed and pushed. feature-compose already refuses exactly this using a shared deterministic helper, and this patcher does not call it.

Make exactly two edits. Each anchor occurs exactly once in the file; copy it verbatim.

EDIT 1 - add the import. Anchor on this exact line:

  import type { ResolverResult } from "./types.js";

and add a line directly after it:

  import { vacuousEditReason } from "../vacuous-edit.js";

EDIT 2 - run the check immediately before staging. Anchor on this exact line:

  // Stage the modified file into a mitosis dir for the cutover machinery.

and replace it with the check followed by that same comment line:

  // DETERMINISTIC VACUOUS-EDIT GATE, UNCONDITIONAL. The region gate above is skipped
  // whenever the proposal names no region, which is most of them, leaving typecheck as
  // the only substantive check on a path that self-lands. vacuousEditReason refuses only
  // when EVERY added line is a declaration whose identifier is never used in the result,
  // so it cannot judge responsiveness and cannot false-block on load - it is a statement
  // about the edit's own text. Same helper feature-compose already uses.
  {
    const vacuous = vacuousEditReason(baseContent, afterSrc);
    if (vacuous) {
      await resetTarget();
      return structuredError("vacuous_edit", {
        target_file: pointer.target_file,
        detail: vacuous,
        before_sha: beforeSha,
        after_sha: afterSha,
      });
    }
  }

  // Stage the modified file into a mitosis dir for the cutover machinery.

Mirror the region gate's own refusal shape exactly: it calls await resetTarget() and returns structuredError(...) with before_sha and after_sha, and all of baseContent, afterSrc, resetTarget, structuredError, beforeSha and afterSha are already in scope at that point.

Change nothing else. Do not alter the region-containment block, the egress gate, or the staging code below.

